0,Arawakan languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arawakan_languages,"Arawakan, also known as Maipurean (also Maipuran), is a language family spoken amongst various Indigenous peoples in South America. Branches migrated to Central America and the Greater Antilles and Lesser Antilles in the Caribbean and the Atlantic, including what is now the Bahamas.",Terêna,Maipurean
1,Ta-Arawakan languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ta-Arawakan_languages,"The Ta-Arawakan languages, also known as Ta-Maipurean and Caribbean, are the Indigenous Arawakan languages of the Caribbean islands and mostly coastal South America.",Terêna,Maipurean
2,Terêna language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Terêna_language,"Terêna or Etelena is an Arawakan language spoken by 15,000 Terenas. The language has a dictionary and written grammar.",Terêna,Maipurean
